Upstream sources and local adaptation boundaries:
- codex-rs/tui/src/external_editor.rs: editor command parsing and external-editor
  handoff/readback policies adapted in exarch/src/tui/terminal.rs and
  ral/src/repl/external_editor.rs.
- codex-rs/tui/src/bottom_pane/textarea.rs and textarea/editing.rs: kill/yank
  and grapheme-boundary editing policies adapted in
  exarch/src/tui/prompt/editor/editing.rs.
- codex-rs/tui/src/bottom_pane/chat_composer/history_search.rs: reverse-history
  search interaction adapted in exarch/src/tui/prompt.rs and
  exarch/src/tui/prompt/search.rs.
- codex-rs/tui/src/bottom_pane/paste_burst.rs: unbracketed-paste classification
  adapted in exarch/src/tui/paste_burst.rs.

These are modified derivatives, not unmodified copies: editor integration uses
ral's authority/transport and exarch's terminal/draft ownership; editing uses
exarch's editor wrapper; search keeps the draft untouched until acceptance and
uses local bounded history. Codex execution and command semantics are not imported.
The Codex-derived portions remain Apache-2.0-only; the workspace's MIT OR
Apache-2.0 licensing does not offer an MIT alternative for those portions.
